  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a3d2b5e5b8bd75781820de5be38f0970, type: 3}
  m_Name: ExhibitData_telescope
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ExhibitData
  exhibitName: THE TELESCOPE
  pages:
  - "For most of human history, the night sky was a mystery.\nStars and planets were
    just tiny dots of light,\nand no one knew what they really were.\n \nThen in
    1608, a Dutch spectacle maker named\nHans Lippershey pointed two lenses at the
    sky\nand suddenly the moon had mountains!\nGalileo heard about it and built his
    own,\ndiscovering that Jupiter had its very own moons\norbiting around it. Mind.
    Blown."
  - "Galileo got in serious trouble for what he saw\nbecause his discoveries proved
    the Earth moved\naround the Sun, not the other way around.\nThe powerful people
    of his time did not like that!\n \nToday the James Webb Space Telescope floats
    in space\nand can see galaxies that formed over 13 billion years ago.\nWe went
    from a simple tube with glass\nto a time machine pointed at the beginning of
    the universe! \U0001F52D"
  exhibitIllustration: {fileID: -4167663028475635082, guid: dc2d958fec53a59d9935bef1308077f6, type: 3}
  narratorClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8cc06d9208d1d89ec8849e5f311ad625, type: 3}
